<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls to 3.35 pct in Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls to 3.35 pct in Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Friday as the issue was oversubscribed, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue fell to 3.35 percent from 3.48 percent at Thursday's auction, 3.59 percent on Wednesday and 3.69 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p>Issue number		  BG3037697003</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     24,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 9</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 7</p>
<p> Bids received		 36,233.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.73 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 23,014.7 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.76 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.35 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
